WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.820
Four times a year, our Masters students put their work on stage at Demo Quarter.

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.974
I'm Thandiwe Solberg, and I convene it.

00:00:09.274 --> 00:00:12.024
I study what happens before the work reaches the stage.

00:00:12.624 --> 00:00:14.314
The rehearsal that gets cut.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:17.633
The one number chosen to stand for a whole sprint.

00:00:17.933 --> 00:00:19.893
The version judged fit to show.

00:00:20.693 --> 00:00:22.253
I study other shows, too.

00:00:22.553 --> 00:00:24.233
The judging at a country show.

00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:25.903
A standing ovation.

00:00:26.203 --> 00:00:28.060
Even the daily stand-up meeting.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:32.150
And her own research has found a wide audience.

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.740
Nine hundred and seventy-three citations,

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:37.940
and an h-index of twenty-five.

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.740
I love the moment the work goes on stage.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.960
I want to know what stayed in the wings.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.310
Her full record is on our website.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.714
Join us on Bluesky,

00:00:47.864 --> 00:00:49.264
or say hello by email.
